@startuml on_behalf_of_block
top to bottom direction

actor "Person" as P
rectangle "Keycloak\nsign-in and token exchange (RFC 8693)" as KC

rectangle "Application built on K9-AIF  (one Keycloak client)" as App {
  rectangle "Router\nadmit(): verify the sign-in, keep the token server side,\nsign the identity" as R
  rectangle "Orchestrator\ncarries the verified person through every squad" as O
  rectangle "Squad  ->  Agent" as A
  rectangle "MCP connector\non_behalf_of: {audience: <MCP server>}" as C
}

rectangle "MCP server\nvalidates the token (addressed to itself)\ndecides from the person's roles" as M

P --> KC : 1. sign in
P --> R : 2. request + token
R --> O : signed identity
O --> A
A --> C : tool call
C --> KC : 3. exchange the token
KC --> C : short-lived token\nperson + this server
C --> M : 4. call with that token

note right of M
  No verified person, or the exchange
  is refused: the call does not run.
  Never a shared key.
end note
@enduml
